{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:740c9de05beddc19","name":"Coruscant Guard","source":{"id":"source:reference-740c9de05beddc19","title":"Coruscant Guard","revision":19410,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:55:12Z","sha256":"a58f8f9f8364668611e890d090b868e30d64d0a27cb40519b468c60b1590b7a1","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19410","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Coruscant%20Guard&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-740c9de05beddc19","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Senate Guard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Senate_Guard","referenceId":"reference:e0e53bb7c97f9801"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Republic","referenceId":"reference:332055cafc4223eb"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One of the status symbols marking ",{"tag":"a","children":["Coruscant"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Coruscant","referenceId":"reference:2ee37a21e9e7a955"}," as the new Imperial Center is the development of an elite Stormtrooper unit specifically for police duty on the capital world. Befitting their unique status, Coruscant Guards wear distinctive red and black armor not issued to regular Stormtrooper or military units. They are afforded great authority to search any dwelling or structure as well as to detain virtually any individual when investigating criminal or subversive activities. High-ranking ",{"tag":"a","children":["ISB Agents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/ISB_Agents"}," might call upon the Guard's services when investigating politically powerful individuals. Although only a few Guard units have been activated, their numbers are growing. Some expect that new units will also appear on important, and potentially disruptive, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Worlds"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Worlds?action=edit&redlink=1"}," in the coming months and years.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Coruscant Guards use their helmet-mounted communications and sensory gear extensively. Commanders use an internal heads-up display to track troop movements and coordinate maneuvers quickly and efficiently. These displays are also useful for navigating Imperial Center's complex city structure.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Coruscant Guard Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6/",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 3; ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"},":"]}," 5\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +10; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"},